summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Follow-up of chronic problems.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Carolyn Smith is a 49-year-old female who presents to the clinic today for follow-up of her chronic problems.

The patient reports that she has been experiencing some osteoarthritis flare-ups, primarily in her elbows. She notes that she has been sitting at a desk for long periods of time at the office, which she believes has increased her flare-ups. She denies any other joint pain. She also reports occasional numbness in her hands when she is typing for long periods of time. She notes that she is right-handed and types all day.

The patient has a history of gout, and her last episode was 3 months ago. She reports that she was treated with medication at that time and has not had any flare-ups since.

The patient also reports that she has psoriasis, which is controlled with medication.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Musculoskeletal: Reports osteoarthritis flare-ups in her elbows. Denies any other joint pain.
Neurological: Reports occasional numbness in her hands.

PHYSICAL EXAM

CV: No cervical lymphadenopathy. Regular rate and rhythm.
RESPIRATORY: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.
MSK: Examination of the right elbow: Edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. Tenderness and effusion present. Pain with pronation and supination. Pain with flexion and extension of the right arm. No lower extremity edema.
GI: Abdomen is soft.

RESULTS

Autoimmune profile is within normal limits. ESR is within normal limits. Uric acid is within normal limits.

ASSESSMENT

1. Gout, stable.
2. Osteoarthritis of the right elbow.
3. Psoriasis, stable.

PLAN

After reviewing the patient's examination and laboratory results today, I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient in regard to her current symptoms. I have recommended that we obtain an x-ray of her right elbow to evaluate the extent of her osteoarthritis. I have also recommended that we continue her on colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed for flare-ups of her gout. Additionally, I have recommended that we start her on meloxicam 15 mg once a day for her pain and swelling. She will follow up with me in 2 weeks to review the results of her x-ray and to assess her symptoms. I have also recommended that we continue her on the steroid cream for her psoriasis.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up with me in 2 weeks.
 }}<|eot_id|>
