summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Left elbow pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Anna Nguyen is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease, who presents with joint pain.

The patient reports left elbow pain. She states that she sits at her desk a lot for work and type and stay in motion specifically all day. After work, it is hard for her to open and close her left elbow. She has noticed swelling there. She is right-handed. She denies numbness or tingling in her hands. She has a little bit of weakness in her arm but nothing too significant. She denies any fever or chills.

Regarding her epilepsy, she reports that she has not had any recent seizures. She is still taking Keppra. She believes her last seizure was a year ago. She is still seeing a therapist, which she found helpful. She is trying to avoid medication since she is already on Keppra. She denies any suicidal or homicidal ideation.

Regarding her depression, she reports that she is doing better with therapy. She still feels a little down and stressed. She denies any suicidal or homicidal ideation.

Regarding her peptic ulcer disease, she reports that she had a lot of stress a year ago. She underwent an endoscopy at that time. She reports that she has not had any issues with her ulcer since then.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fever or chills.
• Musculoskeletal: Endorses left elbow pain.
• Respiratory: Endorses nasal congestion from allergies.
• Neurological: Denies numbness or tingling in her hands. Denies weakness in her arm.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

• Musculoskeletal: Examination of the left elbow: Erythema and edema of the left elbow. Pain with palpation of the olecranon. Warm to palpation. Pain with flexion and extension of the left elbow. Palpable right radial pulse.

RESULTS

X-ray of the left arm was reviewed and demonstrated no evidence of an elbow fracture.

Endoscopy was reviewed and demonstrated gastritis.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Anna Nguyen is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease, who presents with left elbow pain.

Olecranon bursitis.
• Medical Reasoning: She reports pain in her left elbow, which is associated with swelling and stiffness, and pain with movement. Her x-ray did not reveal any fractures.
• Additional Testing: Imaging studies have been ordered.
• Medical Treatment: Rest and a pillow for support. Meloxicam 15 mg, oral, once daily.

Epilepsy.
• Medical Reasoning: She is doing well on her current medication. She has not had any recent seizures.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Keppra 500 mg, oral, twice daily.

Depression.
• Medical Reasoning: She is doing well with therapy and is open to medical treatment options.
• Medical Treatment: Lexapro 10 mg, oral, once daily.

Peptic ulcer disease.
• Medical Reasoning: Her endoscopy revealed gastritis.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg, oral, once daily before meals.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
