Mrs. Lee is a 40-year-old female who presents today for evaluation of back pain. The onset of her pain occurred today. She was at a birthday party where she was surprised and fell down the stairs. She reports that she rammed her back into the railing. She denies any pain radiating down her legs. The pain is localized to her lower back and is worse with lying flat and twisting motions.

PAST HISTORY

Medical
Anxiety.

SURGICAL
Lumbar fusion.

SOCIAL
Patient reports she was at a birthday party today.

MEDICATIONS
