The patient states she has been feeling tired, lacking energy, and having swollen joints in her elbows. She also reports body aches. She recalls she was out hiking in the woods a couple of weeks ago and thought that is where she got the bite. The patient also notes she has been feeling nauseous and has had a poor appetite. She states she has been eating mostly toast and crackers.

The patient reports she had a rash on her abdomen. She describes it as a bull's-eye rash. She denies any high fevers.

Regarding her type 2 diabetes, she states her blood sugars have been running okay, especially now that she has this acute illness. She is still taking metformin. The patient is monitoring her blood sugars at home and reports they have been running a little high and low.

Regarding her hypertension, the patient states she is still taking lisinopril. She has been monitoring her blood pressure at home and reports it has been running well. She has been avoiding salty foods.

The patient states she has been feeling fatigued and has been lacking energy. She denies abdominal pain, diarrhea, or any other symptoms.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Reports fatigue, lack of energy.
