Hannah Smith is a 52-year-old female who presents to the clinic today for evaluation of high blood sugar.

The patient states she has been consuming a lot of sweets lately with the holidays. She notes she felt fine at first, but after a couple of weeks she began to feel lightheaded and was seeing spots. She went to the emergency room and they stated she had high blood sugar. She wanted to follow up with me to get rechecked.

The patient states she is feeling well at this time. She was given IV fluids in the emergency room and was advised to cut out extra sweets and get back into her normal routine, but she is still staying with her family and her mother and grandmother are big bakers so she thinks it will be hard to get into a routine.

