summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Follow-up for asthma, allergic rhinitis and food allergy.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Emily Hernandez is a 20-year-old female who presents for her yearly follow-up for asthma, allergic rhinitis, and food allergy. The patient last visited the office via telemedicine in 2020. She reports that she was switched from Symbicort to Wixela due to insurance changes. She uses Zyrtec in the spring, summer, and fall, which she states works well for her seasonal allergy symptoms. She also has a known peanut allergy and reports she tolerates almonds and cashews. She is trying to reduce her inhaler use for military enlistment. She states she rarely uses her albuterol inhaler and only needs it before strenuous activities.

The patient reports that she completed a breathing test today and had a FEV1 of 91% of predicted, FEV1/FVC of 85%, and PEFR of 85% of predicted. She also reports that she has been trying to reduce her smoking and vaping use. She has had some episodes of vaping and smoking over the past year but has been trying to cut back. She states she has not had any issues with her asthma over the past year and denies any urgent care or ER visits for breathing issues.

Allergy History
Peanut
Almond
Cashew

CURRENT MEDICATIONS

Albuterol inhaler
Zyrtec
Wixela

