• Respiratory: Denies dyspnea on exertion. Reports rare use of rescue inhaler.
• ENT: Reports seasonal allergies.
• Allergic/Immunologic: Reports peanut allergy.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Respiratory: Normal respiratory effort, clear to auscultation bilaterally.

RESULTS

Spirometry: FEV1 of 91% of predicted, FEV1/FVC of 85%, PEFR of 85% of predicted.

ASSESSMENT

• Mild intermittent asthma.
• Allergic rhinitis.
• Peanut allergy.

PLAN

After reviewing the patient's examination and spirometry results today, I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient in regards to her current asthma regimen. She is currently on Wixela and has been using it once a day. She is rarely using her albuterol inhaler. I have recommended that we step down her inhaler to Alvesco, 80 mcg, 2 puffs twice a day. She will continue to use her albuterol inhaler as needed and her EpiPen. She will discontinue her Wixela. We will repeat spirometry in 4 months. She will follow-up with me in 4 months for repeat spirometry and ACT.

