summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Irritable Bowel Syndrome with functional abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Brittany Edwards is a 32-year-old female who is a return visit for Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) with flares of abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting. The patient was last seen in August 2019 with flares of abdominal pain who was diagnosed with IBS and treated with Bentyl. She had a previous prescription for Reglan that she received from the emergency room which she used as needed for nausea. She was instructed to start a low-dose fiber supplement, such as psyllium, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, Bentyl up to four times daily for intestinal cramping, and to stop Reglan and use Zofran as needed. Neuromodulators such as Elavil and Buspar were discussed but not started.

The patient reports that she has been going out to eat on Friday nights and Saturday nights and has had some spicy foods or spicy shrimp. Her gut does not appreciate these foods as well.

She states she is starting to notice bowel movements between 2-3 times a day. They are formed stools. After she goes out to eat with her friends, she tends to have diarrhea. She does not feel it is the food or the alcohol, but both.

The patient denies any issues with her bowel movements when she is not eating out. She has had fried chicken today and it was well tolerated. She notes that she usually does not have any issues with pasta, grilled chicken, or Patron. She prefers Patron over brown liquor and will only drink 2 drinks. She will occasionally drink a martini.

When she is not eating out or drinking, her bowel movements are regular. She is advised to continue using psyllium and probiotics daily. She will take Bentyl 20 mg before eating at a restaurant. She can take Zofran as needed.

The patient was advised to watch the portion sizes. She can not go out without eating some fried chicken at least once in a while.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Constitutional: Alert and cooperative, appears stated age.

Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.

Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm.

Gastrointestinal: Soft, non-tender. No masses or organomegaly. Normal active bowel sounds.

RESULTS

None.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Brittany Edwards is a pleasant 32-year-old female with Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) with functional abdominal pain, aggravated by high stress, poor eating habits, and poor sleeping habits.

• Irritable Bowel Syndrome with functional abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting.
• Medical Reasoning: She is having moderate to severe symptoms. Her symptoms are being aggravated by high stress, poor eating habits, and poor sleeping habits.
• Medical Treatment: I encouraged dietary and lifestyle modifications, as well as starting a neuromodulator such as Elavil 25 mg at bedtime for IBS. She can use Bentyl 20 mg as needed 30-45 minutes prior to eating out at a restaurant. She can also use Zofran if needed. I have encouraged her to reduce greasy and fatty foods and alcohol consumption.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 1 month by email over MyChart regarding any side effects and issues with Elavil or if adjustments are needed. }}<|eot_id|>
