Tyler Nelson is a 72-year-old male who presents for follow-up for ongoing management of rheumatoid arthritis. The patient reports that he received a steroid injection in his right knee last time he was here, but the swelling has persisted. The patient states that the injection provided temporary relief for about 2 weeks. The patient reports that he has had persistent swelling and pain in the right knee for approximately 2 months. The patient states that he also has swelling in the right leg. He rates his pain as 6 out of 10 on a normal day, and 3 out of 10 currently. The patient states that the swelling has been present since his last visit, about 2 months ago. The patient reports that he has slowed down his activities and has found ways to quickly get up from a seated position. He states that he uses a cane for support when getting up from a seated position.

The patient has been compliant with his medication regimen, including Xeljanz 11 mg daily and Celebrex 200 mg daily, which he started 2 months ago.

