X-ray of the right knee has been ordered.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Tyler Nelson is a 72-year-old male who presents for follow-up of rheumatoid arthritis. He continues to have significant right knee pain and swelling, despite treatment. The patient received a steroid injection in the right knee today.

Diagnosis: Rheumatoid Arthritis with right knee pain and swelling.
1. Right knee pain and swelling.
   - Medical Reasoning: The patient reports that the swelling has been present for 2 months, and has not improved with his current treatment regimen. The patient received a steroid injection today.
