Barbara Johnson is a 31-year-old female who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of abdominal pain.

The patient reports that she has been experiencing abdominal pain for the past week. She has a longstanding history of diabetes mellitus type 2 and asthma. She notes that her pain is increasing in severity. She also reports associated nausea and vomiting. She notes that she has experienced nausea approximately 3 times in the past week. She also reports vomiting a couple of times. She states that she has been drinking a lot of coffee lately. She notes that her pain is located bilaterally in her upper abdomen. The patient also notes that her pain increases when she exercises.

The patient denies fever.

MEDICAL HISTORY

The patient reports that she has a history of diabetes mellitus type 2. She also reports that she has asthma.

MEDICATIONS

The patient reports that she is taking metformin 500 mg once a day. She also reports that she is taking flovent twice a day and albuterol as needed.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Denies fever.
Gastrointestinal: Endorses abdominal pain. Endorses nausea. Endorses vomiting.
Respiratory: Denies dyspnea. Endorses wheezing.

