Respiratory
• Auscultation of Lungs: Clear to auscultation/normal.
• Examination of Lungs: Mild expiratory wheezes.

Cardiovascular
• Auscultation of Heart: Grade 3/6 systolic ejection murmur, unchanged from prior exam.

Gastrointestinal
• Examination of Abdomen: Mild tenderness in the epigastrium. Abdomen otherwise soft. No tenderness in the right lower quadrant. No significant tenderness in the right upper quadrant.

RESULTS

We will check a urinalysis, urine pregnancy test, CBC, and CMP.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Acute gastritis without bleeding.
• Medical Reasoning: I believe that the patient's abdominal pain is likely due to acute gastritis. She reports drinking a lot of coffee and consuming spicy foods, which may be contributing to her symptoms.
• Medical Treatment: I will prescribe Zantac 150 mg twice a day.

Diabetes Mellitus type 2.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has a longstanding history of diabetes mellitus type 2. She is currently taking metformin 500 mg twice a day. Her blood sugar levels are currently under control.
• Medical Treatment: I will increase her dose of metformin to 1000 mg in the morning and 500 mg in the evening.

Asthma.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has a history of asthma. She is currently taking Flovent twice a day and albuterol as needed. She denies wheezing.
